        "title": "Supper with Dad",
        "properties": {
          "title": "Supper with Dad",
          "location": "Dining Room",
          "charactersPresent": "",
          "text": "Dad sits at the head of the table. Across from him, the Effigy, its sack head turned slightly toward you.\nDad: Sit. Eat. Your mother's watching.\nYou eat the gray soup. It tastes like pennies.\nDad: The Last Supper is coming. The sabbath. When it's laid out, this house will be consecrated, and she'll be whole.\nDad: But the dust is getting thicker. I need to see farther in the dark.\nDad: Out in the corn there's a battery, a wire, and a mirror. Bring them to me and I'll make you a flashlight.\nDad: You'll have ten minutes before the Night Crusher comes for you. Don't make him carry you home.",
          "audioLoop": "",
          "audioLoopName": "",
          "audioOneShot": "",
          "audioOneShotName": "",
          "background": "",
          "backgroundName": "",
          "showCharacterImages": true,
