        "title": "The Flashlight",
        "properties": {
          "title": "The Flashlight",
          "location": "Dining Room",
          "charactersPresent": "",
          "text": "You stumble in the back door, coated in dust, arms full.\nDad lays the battery, the wire, and the mirror on the table beside the Effigy's empty plate.\nHis soot-black fingers twist and solder. A beam of white light cuts through the dust in the room.\nDad: Good job. This is your flashlight. Use it sparingly, because the dark notices light.\nHe turns the beam across the Effigy's blank burlap face.\nDad: Your mother needs eyes. And teeth. We'll talk about that tomorrow.",
