  "varMeta": {
    "characters": {
      "Boy": {
        "info": "A four-year-old in an oversized flannel nightshirt and scuffed boots, hair full of dust, eyes too large for his narrow face. He is small enough to slip between cornstalks and under car wrecks. Rendered as a simple bold silhouette, pale against the dark."
      },
      "Dad": {
        "info": "A tall, gaunt man in a stained leather apron over a Depression-era waistcoat, sleeves rolled to the elbow, forearms blackened with soot. Round smoked-glass spectacles hide his eyes. He moves little and speaks as if reciting scripture or a recipe. Half father, half warlock-alchemist."
      },
      "Effigy": {
        "info": "A crude life-size figure of the Boy's missing mother propped in a high-backed chair. Its body is a dress form stuffed with straw and wrapped in a faded floral housedress. The head is a burlap sack with no features yet. Empty spaces where eyes, teeth and hands should be are marked with pins and chalk."
      },
      "Night Crusher": {
        "info": "A hulking chthonic shape, taller than the cornstalks, made of packed earth, root and coal dust, with a long stooped back. Its face is a smooth blank of clay with a single horizontal crack. It drags one enormous hand along the ground and leaves a furrow behind it. It is seen mostly in silhouette, black against black."
      }
    },
    "locations": {
      "The Closet": {
        "info": "A narrow coat closet under the stairs where the Boy sleeps on a folded quilt. Moth-eaten coats hang overhead like sleeping bats. A thin blade of yellow light comes under the door. The walls feel slightly farther apart each time he wakes."
      },
      "Dining Room": {
        "info": "A long farmhouse table under a single bare bulb, set with mismatched plates and a tureen of something gray. Dust sifts constantly through the window frames. At the head of the table sits Dad, and across from him sits the Effigy. Alchemical glassware crowds the sideboard."
      },
      "Back Field": {
        "info": "A flat expanse of Dust Bowl Kansas behind the house, black and white like an old photograph, with dust hanging in the air like fog. A dim orange glow sits on the horizon. Very far off, impossibly bright, a gleaming white house stands alone in the field. It never seems to get closer."
      },
      "Corn Maze": {
        "info": "High dead corn and wheat, taller than a man, rattling in the wind, with narrow rows that twist back on themselves. Scarecrows stand at odd intervals, some tilted, some face-down. Visibility is a few feet at most. Pools of faint light come from nowhere in particular."
      },
      "The Crash": {
        "info": "A clearing at the heart of the maze where several 1930s cars have collided and rusted together into one heap: a pickup, a sedan, a delivery truck on its side. Dozens of scarecrows are piled and crushed among the wreckage, their straw gone gray, as if they have been out here for years."
      },
      "Night Crusher's Burrow": {
        "info": "A low earthen chamber beneath the yard, lit by a smoldering coal seam in the wall. Roots hang from the ceiling. In one corner lies a thin pallet with a clean white sheet, oddly cared-for. It is quiet down here, like being inside a held breath."
      }
    }
  },
  "projectTitle": "Night of the Night Crusher",
  "bookmarks": []
